/*!
* @defgroup tmr System Timer Module (TMR)
* @ingroup tmr
* @brief The S32 SDK provides Peripheral Drivers for the System Timer Module (TMR).
*
* The System Timer Module (TMR) is a 32-bit timer designed to support commonly required
* system and application software timing functions. The TMR includes a 32-bit up counter and
* four 32-bit compare channels with a separate interrupt source for each channel
*
* The number of TMR instances depends on the number of cores of MCU device, one for each core,
* with four 32-bit compare channels in each TMR
* 
* ## Hardware background ##
*
* The TMR has the following features:
*     - One 32-bit up counter with 8-bit prescaler
*     - Four 32-bit compare channels
*     - Independent interrupt source for each channel 
*     - Counter can be stopped in debug mode 
*     - TMR runs on the system clock by default
*
* 
* ## Integration guideline ##
*
* ### Compilation units ###
*
* The following files need to be compiled in the project:
* \verbatim
${S32SDK_PATH}\platform\drivers\src\tmr\tmr_driver.c
\endverbatim
*
* ### Include path ###
*
* The following paths need to be added to the include path of the toolchain:
* \verbatim
${S32SDK_PATH}\platform\drivers\inc\
\endverbatim
*
* ### Preprocessor symbols ###
*
* No special symbols are required for this component
* 
* ### Dependencies ###
\ref clock_manager \n
* 
*/
